# Database migrations

Use the `DATABASE_URL` from `.env` and run migrations from the repository root:

```bash
set -a && . ./.env && set +a
uv run alembic upgrade head
uv run alembic current
uv run alembic check
```

For local development, start the Compose PostgreSQL service first:

```bash
docker compose -f compose.yml up -d postgres
```

After upgrading, seed the deterministic Free/Pro plans and demo tenant with
`uv run python -m app.data.seed`. Do not edit generated revisions after they
have been applied; create a new revision for future schema changes.